        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(web): declutter shell chrome like Slack",
        "body": "Declutters the shell chrome so the desktop app reads like a native client (Slack-style) instead of stacking duplicate controls.\n\n## Problem\n\n- Two settings buttons: a gear in the Electron title bar (opened desktop settings) and a gear in the sidebar workspace header (opened workspace settings).\n- \"Connected\" shown twice, permanently: a pill in the title bar and a status line under the workspace name.\n- The workspace name also appeared twice on desktop (title bar + sidebar header).\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Desktop title bar**: now holds only the sidebar toggle and the centered search. App settings remain reachable natively via the app menu, `Cmd/Ctrl+,`, and the tray menu (all pre-existing).\n- **Sidebar header**: the workspace name is now a menu button with a chevron that opens workspace settings, replacing the separate gear.\n- **Connection state**: no steady-state indicator. A pulsing \"Connecting…\" line appears under the workspace name only while the realtime link is down (respects `prefers-reduced-motion`). The shell exposes `data-connected` for readiness probes.\n- E2E readiness checks moved from `getByText(\"Connected\")` to `.shell[data-connected=\"true\"]`; docs and changelog updated; embedded web assets refreshed.\n\n## Proof\n\nDesktop chrome after (title bar: toggle + centered search only; sidebar: workspace name menu, no duplicate status):\n\n![desktop shell chrome](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openclaw/clickclack/claude/settings-ui-native-redesign-ae565b/docs/proof/shell-chrome-desktop-titlebar.png)\n\n- `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm fmt:ts:check`, `pnpm build` all green.\n- Targeted e2e: 9/9 passed (desktop titlebar layout, Windows caption-control space, native-frame fallback, realtime connection state, app-subdomain boot, sidebar collapse, notification flows).\n- Autoreview (Codex gpt-5.6-sol, xhigh): clean, no actionable findings.\n",
